        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "Explain why you cannot prove $\\sin n\\cot n=\\cos n$ using mathematical induction.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Here $n$ is an angle, not an integer index. Induction would not establish the identity for every angle where it is defined.",
          "worked": "The identity concerns all angles for which $\\cot n$ is defined. A base case and a step from $k$ to $k+1$ cover only a sequence of values, so they do not prove the identity for every such angle.",
